/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A baseband link sends one symbol every T seconds.
   - The transmit filter gT(t), the channel c(t) and the receive filter gR(t) shape the pulse.
   - r(t) = Σ an p(t − nT) + n(t)
   - Here r(t) is the waveform reaching the sampler, the sum runs over every symbol n, and n(t) is the noise.
   - Sample at t = kT to decide symbol k.
   - y(kT) = ak p(0) + Σn≠k an p((k − n)T) + n(kT)
   - Here the first term is the wanted one, the middle sum is the ISI, and n(kT) is the noise sample.
   - The ISI depends on the samples p(±T), p(±2T), … of the overall pulse.
   - Make every ISI term zero: require p(0) ≠ 0 and p(nT) = 0 for every integer n ≠ 0.
   - In frequency the same condition reads: the spectrum P(f), copied at every multiple of 1/T and added, must be flat.
*/
