/* book exam traps: Using Rs where Rs/2 belongs. The minimum bandwidth is half the symbol rate: 2400 baud needs 1200 Hz, not 2400 Hz. | Mixing bit rate and symbol rate. BN = Rs/2 uses the symbol rate; for 4-PAM at 4800 bit/s, Rs = 2400 baud and BN = 1200 Hz. | Dropping the signs in the ISI sum. ISI adds with the sign of each neighbour; only the peak distortion uses magnitudes. | Writing the criterion as p(t) = 0 for t ≠ 0. It is only at the instants t = nT; between them the pulse is free. */
