/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - The criterion asks that the copies of P(f), spaced 1/T apart, add up to a constant.
   - B = (Rs/2)(1 + α)
   - Here B is the baseband bandwidth in hertz, Rs = 1/T is the symbol rate in baud and α is the roll-off factor, 0 ≤ α ≤ 1.
   - excess bandwidth = B − Rs/2 = αRs/2
   - Here α is the excess as a fraction of the Nyquist bandwidth: α = 0.25 spends 25 % more than Rs/2.
   - α = 0 is the sinc with B = Rs/2. α = 1 doubles the band to B = Rs and gives the gentlest filter.
   - p(t) = sinc(t/T) · cos(παt/T) / [1 − (2αt/T)²]
   - Here sinc(x) = sin(πx)/(πx), so p(0) = 1.
   - Where the bracket is zero, at t = ±T/(2α), the formula reads 0/0 and the limit is p = (π/4)·sinc(1/(2α)).
   - The tails decide practical success.
*/
