/* book exam traps: Dropping the half: writing B = Rs(1 + α) or excess = αRs. The correct forms are B = (Rs/2)(1 + α) and excess = αRs/2. | Putting the bit rate where the symbol rate belongs. For M-PAM use Rs = Rb/log₂M in the bandwidth formula. | Choosing α = 0 because it is the narrowest. The brick wall cannot be built and its eye closes under the smallest timing error; justify a practical α of 0.2 to 0.5. | Expecting one root raised cosine filter to give zero ISI. Only the transmit and receive RRC filters in cascade make the raised cosine. */
